+## Stored ID validation increment — 25 October 2026
+
+Increment 14 combines the existing whitespace/control checks without changing accepted identifiers, Unicode length limits, error paths, JSON/schema/reference validation or stored formats. Complete dense-state validation improves by 12–14% in two alternating comparisons; 3,342,349 differential ID checks match the original. This is a CPU improvement only. The fresh five-account API diagnostic still misses the one-second gate: 10/10 accepted, p95 1,486.4 ms before and 1,498.7 ms after. Exact replay, all history/XP and cleanup pass in both. Desktop durable check medians are 283.2/327.0/566.0 ms (Chromium/WebKit/Firefox); single production DOM-feedback samples are 122.6/114.0/193.0 ms. These remain above target and are not physical/p95 acceptance.
